      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle by Completing the Square",
      "problem": "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${y}^{2}-8x-10y+{x}^{2}=8.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-8x-10y+{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-8x)+({y}^{2}-10y) & =8 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =8+{4}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={7}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(4,5)$ and its radius is $7.$",
