      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 selected answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. For q-117086 and q-70933, standard circle form gives centers (7,10) and (-1,-6), with radii 10 and 4. For q-72621 and q-117096, squared distances from center to circumference are 16+25=41 and 9+9=18. For q-117102 and q-117107, diameter midpoints are (2,2) and (1,-1), and squared radii are 4 and 8. Completing squares gives q-5183: (x-4)^2+(y-5)^2=49; q-15456: (x+12)^2+(y+3)^2=16, so a+b+r=-11; q-76374: (x-1)^2+(y-1/4)^2=9/16; q-103892: (x+7/2)^2+y^2=49/4. The visible ellipse intercepts give squared semiaxes (9,1), (1,4), and (4,36) for q-69891, q-69892, and q-115124. Full axis lengths are twice the semiaxes, giving (6√2,6) for q-7596 and (14,12) for q-115134. For q-70479, the image lacks readable axes and coordinates, so its geometry cannot be independently verified from the image; however, its captured solution explicitly supplies center (-1,1), semiaxes 3 and 1, and the matching equation. No mathematical disagreement with the captured solutions is demonstrated.",
