      "worked_solution": "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+7x & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+7x)+{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}x+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2})+{y}^{2} & ={(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-\\frac{7}{2}))}^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-\\frac{7}{2},0)$ and its radius is $\\frac{7}{2}.$",
